Description
You are tasked with creating a new table for managing book information in a library system.
The table should be named books and include columns for book_id (integer and primary key),
title (string up to 255 characters), author (string up to 100 characters), and published_year (datetime).
Task: Write the SQL command to create this table.

CREATE TABLE books (
 book_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
 title VARCHAR(255),
 author VARCHAR(100),
 published_year DATETIME
 );



Description
After a review, you decide to remove all books published before the year 2000 from the books table. 
(Assuming we added back the published_year column for this scenario.)
Task: Write the SQL command to delete all records of books published before the year 2000.

DELETE FROM books
 WHERE  published_year < '2000-01-01';

Description
After some time, you realize that the books table should also include a column for the genre of the book
which should be a string up to 50 characters.
Task: Write the SQL command to add a genre column to the books table.

 ALTER TABLE books
 ADD genre VARCHAR(50);


